{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:eaa46ac548b28f78","name":"Medic (CL 3)","source":{"id":"source:reference-eaa46ac548b28f78","title":"Medic (CL 3)","revision":25243,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:19:58Z","sha256":"86730c0fc0f87b6551e4f78653f273e7a9ca3a04f76173280a240694c57603a3","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25243","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Medic%20%28CL%203%29&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-eaa46ac548b28f78","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When a soldier falls in battle, it is the duty of the Medic to tend to them there or drag him or her back from the front lines to the field hospital. What separates a Medic from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Doctor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Doctor","referenceId":"reference:24669ff48290c187"}," is that a Medic receives rudimentary combat training to enable them to fight alongside their companions against enemy forces. Although possessed of some combat ability, a Medic is not an ideal fighter and spends most of their time tending to the wounded. \n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Medic Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medics are attached to military units, usually in a ratio of one Medic for every dozen or so soldiers, more or less depending on the quality of the unit. Mercenary companies have fewer trained Medics than other combat groups, leaving most mercenaries to tend to their own wounds.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Medic is an important and valued member of any outfit. Since the Medic's main responsibility is saving lives, most units don't risk their Medics without good reason. In fact, soldiers often take risks to keep their unit's Medic safe, even exposing themselves to gunfire to deal with a threat to the Medic. In exchange, the soldiers expect the Medic to move quickly when one of the team falls. While the Medic applies a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Medpac"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Medpac","referenceId":"reference:f89e0de3ab0ae989"},", the rest of the team provides covering fire until the Medic and his injured patient can return to cover.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Medic Statistics (CL 3)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6/",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 5\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, 1 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 15 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 15), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 13, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 29, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Thresho